  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Olof Palme Center - Supporting Inclusive Democratic Transition in DRC - Palme Center - Supporting Inclusive Democratic Transition in DRC</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Palmecentret - st&#xf6;d till inkluderande demokratiska maktskiften i DRK</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Projektet har utformats efter ett f&#xf6;rsta f&#xf6;rstudiebes&#xf6;k i Kinshasa f&#xf6;r att bed&#xf6;ma m&#xf6;jligheterna f&#xf6;r ett projekt f&#xf6;r att st&#xf6;dja inkluderande och demokratisk &#xf6;verg&#xe5;ng i Demokratiska republiken Kongo. Det &#xf6;vergripande m&#xe5;let f&#xf6;r programmet &#xe4;r &quot;h&#xe5;llbara civilsamh&#xe4;llesorganisationer som deltar i breda allianser som bidrar till att fr&#xe4;mja god samh&#xe4;llsstyrning, arbetsr&#xe4;tt, medborgarengagemang och kvinnors lika politiska deltagande&quot;.

Programmet har tre komponenter; fackf&#xf6;reningar, medborgarr&#xf6;relser och kvinnoorganisationer, medan den f&#xf6;rsta &#xe4;r den centrala delen av programmet som t&#xe4;cker cirka 50 procent av projektet. De olika komponenterna kommer att inneh&#xe5;lla f&#xf6;ljande:

Fackf&#xf6;reningar: Programmet inkluderar projektfinansiering och kapacitetsst&#xf6;d f&#xf6;r att st&#xe4;rka fackf&#xf6;reningarnas utbildningsvingar och teknisk kunskap om hur man rekryterar nya medlemmar, demokratiskt organiserar och mobiliserar medlemmar och informella arbetare, s&#xe4;rskilt kvinnor, underl&#xe4;ttar alliansbyggande och n&#xe4;tverkande inom fackf&#xf6;reningsr&#xf6;relsen, &#xf6;ver sektorer och internationellt samt st&#xf6;dja utvecklingen av en gemensam plattform som kan bidra till facklig enhet och fr&#xe4;mja social dialog.

Medborgarr&#xf6;relse: Programmet inkluderar projektfinansiering och kapacitetsuppbyggnadsinsatser f&#xf6;r att st&#xf6;dja r&#xf6;relsen att bli mer strategisk och h&#xe5;llbar, f&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttra interna demokratiska strukturer, inklusive temaf&#xe4;rdigheter inom olika tematiska omr&#xe5;den som j&#xe4;mst&#xe4;lldhet, social dialog, organisationsutveckling, riskanalys och lindring &#xe5;tg&#xe4;rder och fr&#xe4;mja samarbete b&#xe5;de inom r&#xf6;relsen och med andra delar av det civila samh&#xe4;llet.

Kvinnors politiska deltagande: Programmet inkluderar projektfinansiering och kapacitetsuppbyggnadsaktiviteter f&#xf6;r att st&#xe4;rka kvinnliga politiker och deras f&#xf6;rm&#xe5;ga att formulera sina politiska intressen, utveckla ideologibaserat politiskt inneh&#xe5;ll och reformer, transparenta och deltagande processer och utbyte med kvinnliga politiker fr&#xe5;n andra l&#xe4;nder.

Palme Center kommer att arbeta tillsammans med partnerorganisationer och medlemsorganisationer f&#xf6;r att driva p&#xe5; en progressiv h&#xe5;llbar utveckling och inkluderande demokrati. Att bygga starka allianser mellan sektorer &#xe4;r viktigt f&#xf6;r att f&#xf6;rverkliga detta.

Programmet kommer att genomf&#xf6;ras genom partnerorganisationer som &#xe4;r aktiva i var och en av de tre komponenterna som kommer att bidra till f&#xf6;rv&#xe4;ntade beteendef&#xf6;r&#xe4;ndringar (resultat) i deras respektive sammanhang. Partnerorganisationerna kommer inte var och en av dem att bidra till alla f&#xf6;rv&#xe4;ntade resultat, men som helhet kommer de att bidra till programmets &#xf6;vergripande m&#xe5;l.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project has been designed after an initial pre-study visit to Kinshasa to assess the possibilities for a project to support inclusive and democratic transition in the DRC. The overall goal of the programme is &quot;sustainable civil society organisations engage in broad alliances that contribute to the advancement of good governance, labour rights, citizens engagement and women&#x2019;s equal political participation&quot;.

The programme has three components; trade unions, citizens movement and women&apos;s organisations, whereas the first one is the central part of the programme covering around 50 percent of the project. The different components will contain the following:

Trade unions: The programme includes project funding and capacity support to strengthen trade unions educational wings and technical knowledge on how to recruit new members, democratically organise and mobilise members and informal workers, particularly women, facilitate alliance building and networking within the trade union movement, cross sectors and internationally and support the development of a common platform that could contribute to trade union unity and promote social dialogue.

Citizens movement: The program includes project funding and capacity building efforts to support the movement to become more strategic and sustainable, improve internal democratic structures, including thematic skills within different thematic areas such as gender equality, social dialogue, organisational development, risk analysis and mitigation measures, and promoting cooperation both within the movement and with other parts of civil society. 

Women&#x2019;s political participation: The program includes project funding and capacity building activities to strengthen women politicians and their capacities to articulate their political interests, develop ideology-based political content and reforms, transparent and participatory processes and exchange with women politicians from other countries.

The Palme Center will work together with partner organisations and member organisations to push for a progressive sustainable development and inclusive democracy. Building strong alliances across sectors is vital to realise this.

The programme will be implemented through partner organisations active in each of the three Components that will contribute to the expected behavioural changes (outcomes) in their respective contexts. The partner organisations will not each of them contribute to all expected outcomes, but as a whole they will contribute to the overall goal of the programme.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This programme focuses on supporting trade unions and civil society organisations engage in broad alliances that contribute to the advancement of good governance, labour rights, citizens engagement and women&apos;s equal political participation. The programme will contribute to Strengthened democracy and gender equality, and greater respect for human rights of the Strategy for Sweden&apos;s development cooperation with the Democratic Republic of the Congo 2015-2019 (prolonged until 2020).

The programme will contribute to:
1.Strengthened democratic institutions and rule of law
2.Increased participation of women in elected decision-making forums
3.Strengthened capacity of civil society to promote transparency, accountability and improved respect for human rights

The overall goal of the programme is the therefore formulated as Sustainable civil society organisations engage in broad alliances that contribute to the
advancement of good governance, labour rights, citizens engagement and women&apos;s equal political participation.</narrative>
  </description>
